\item \textbf{Consent as a Further Limit (\textit{Landor}, 2026):} In \textit{Landor v.\ Louisiana Department of Corrections and Public Safety}, No.~23-1197 (June 23, 2026), the Court held that individuals may not be held personally liable for damages under RLUIPA, a Spending Clause statute. Rejecting the argument that \textit{Dole}'s four requirements are the whole test, Justice Gorsuch's opinion for the Court explained that they ``apply in addition to---not instead of---the rule that Congress may not use the Spending Clause to bind entities and individuals without their knowing and voluntary consent.''
